n't load there in 40s (`gpuLoadTimeout`, well inside the gateway's 2 minutes), or doesn't answer in time there twice in a row, is started on the CPU, and Settings says why; a request it didn't answer in time once is tried on the GPU again, since a slow request on a weak GPU is no lost GPU (#3682). The GPU is tried again 10 minutes later, doubling to 2 hours while it keeps failing, with no restart (`gpuRetryAfter`), and one that answers is the model's again), joins short texts into 12 KB chunks and maps the spans back, cuts a text over 12 KB into pieces of 12 KB at most that overlap by 1 KB (`pieces`: after a line's end, else a space, else at a rune's start), each kept by its own hash, their spans put back at the text's offsets and merged where pieces overlap (`merge`: one found twice is one, one cut by a piece's end is whole), and asks pf-serve a chunk at a time (#3682: a 480 KB text whole took an RX 470/580 90s and kept nothing when cut off), keeps the last 20000 answers by hash, on disk too (`found-<model>.bin` beside the model: hashes, offsets, labels and each span's score, never text; a `pfound01` file from before scores is read with every span sure, so it masks as it did; written through temp-and-rename, a bad read taken as empty), so a restart doesn't ask the model about every history again (#3682), and ends it after 10 minutes with no request. Its requests take turns on its one pipe (`turn`), and a request reads the cache again when its turn comes; a request waits for its turn only while its context lives (`pii.FindContext`, through `gwmw.ContextTeller`), so one whose client went away leaves the queue (the gateway's 2 minutes leave masking's time out, #3682); the chunk pf-serve is on is finished and kept, so a request sent again asks only about what is left, and between chunks the turn is given up and taken again, so a short request goes before the rest of a long one. The status (`pii.Now`), `pii.Stop` and the idle timer never wait for a load or a request: `s